## AI-Assisted

## style-ok: no-strict -- sourced, side-effect-free fragment; a top-level
## 'set -o errexit' etc. would leak into the sourcing shell.

## local_apt_repo_store_ensure: make the LOCAL apt repo store
## (local_apt_repository_base, default /srv/derivative-maker, derived in
## variables.d/05_load-config.bsh) exist, be owned by the build user (user_name)
## and be world-traversable (0755) -- so reprepro writes it UNPRIVILEGED and apt
## reads it with no _apt sandbox note (no 0700-$HOME ancestor). Sourced by
## build-steps.d/1200_prepare-build-machine; also sourced standalone by its unit
## test. Reads user_name, local_apt_repository_base and SUDO_TO_ROOT from the
## environment (all set by help-steps/variables).
local_apt_repo_store_ensure() {
   ## Create unprivileged when the build user can (a store under $HOME it already
   ## owns, or the CI override pointing it back under binary_build_folder_dist).
   ## Failure is fine: a fresh dir under root-owned /srv, or a root-run build, is
   ## corrected below. 'install -d -m' sets the mode on EVERY component it creates
   ## AND re-modes a dir we own (fixing messed-up perms), unlike 'mkdir -p -m'
   ## (deepest only, SC2174) -- so the store and its /srv prefix are
   ## world-traversable for _apt even under a 027 build umask, in one atomic call.
   ## The store is always a DEDICATED directory, so forcing 0755 is safe.
   install -d -m 0755 -- "${local_apt_repository_base}" 2>/dev/null || true

   ## Guarantee final OWNERSHIP + mode. The create above checks CREATION, not
   ## ownership, and leaves the store root:root whenever root created or already
   ## owned it: (a) a root-run build (euid 0) created it root:root, or (b) a
   ## root:root 0755 dir already existed, so 'install -d' succeeded trivially and
   ## skipped the chmod -- and never chowned. reprepro then writes the store
   ## UNPRIVILEGED and fails with Permission denied. Re-run as root with -o/-g to
   ## create-or-fix owner+mode in one idempotent call; skipped entirely when the
   ## build user already owns it (the $HOME fast path -> no sudo).
   # shellcheck disable=SC2086  # SUDO_TO_ROOT is an intentionally word-split command prefix
   if [ "$(stat -c '%U' -- "${local_apt_repository_base}" 2>/dev/null)" != "${user_name}" ]; then
      ${SUDO_TO_ROOT} install -d -m 0755 -o "${user_name}" -g "${user_name}" -- "${local_apt_repository_base}"
   fi
}
